WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.350
If you want to hear about how all five Conjuring
movies to date are referenced in the trailer

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.480
for Annabelle Comes Home then make sure you
watch this whole video.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:12.940
I called it!

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.000
I called it!

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.599
Back in September I did a DeadTalk where I
speculated possible future Conjuring spin-offs.

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:20.949
This is what I had to say about Annabelle
3.

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:25.050
“So my guess is that Annabelle 3 will take
place while the Warrens are away on another

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.650
case, perhaps this takes place at the same
time as The Conjuring 3, and the film will

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.820
focus on Judy, or the nanny who takes care
of her, as horrors start to take place around

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:33.820
the house.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.480
With Ed and Lorraine not there to help, Judy
may have to take on this entity on her own.”

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.940
Cut to: almost everything I just said being
true in the trailer.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.690
Parents lock up the room, they say goodbye
to Judy because they’re going somewhere,

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.440
mistakes happen, and she says she sees things...

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.290
Wait, didn’t I also make a video last year
where I said they could do movies on the whole

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.650
room of cursed objects in the Warren’s home?

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:57.630
“But I think this room of trinkets is a
clever way to tie the series together, and

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.320
we may even see spin-offs of other objects
from this room.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.320
I mean…

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.230
I know I’d watch a movie about this monkey.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.440
Wouldn’t you?”

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.250
Cut back to the Annabelle Comes Home trailer.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.979
The monkey moves!

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:14.119
OK, it’s not it’s own movie like I originally
said, but in a way, having a movie where all

00:01:14.119 --> 00:01:16.659
the haunted objects interact could be even
better.

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:20.189
We may get a little glimpse into the history
of some of these objects, but we won’t get

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:24.329
beat down with a bunch of repetitive spin-offs
that simply go from object to object.

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:27.509
The only part of my prediction that may be
off, is where I said this could take place

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:31.619
at the same time as The Conjuring 3, because
I wasn’t expecting them to recast Judy with

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:32.619
a younger actress.

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:36.350
It looks like this takes place between The
Conjuring and The Conjuring 2, because in

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:40.109
this shot we see the music box from the first
Conjuring, and in the wide shot, you’ll

00:01:40.109 --> 00:01:44.429
notice that the item Ed Warren places there
at the end of The Conjuring 2 is not there

00:01:44.429 --> 00:01:45.429
yet.

00:01:45.429 --> 00:01:49.149
We also see what looks like a genie lamp,
which reminds me of The Conjuring, where Ed

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:53.420
Warren explains that destroying the objects
would just unleash the spirit within them

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.680
and that sometimes it’s better to keep the
genie in the bottle.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.179
"It's safer for these things to be in here
than out there.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.640
It's kind of like keeping weapons off the
streets."

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.200
"Well why not just throw them in an incinerator?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.100
Destroy em?"

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.020
"That would only destroy the vessel.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.099
Sometimes it's better to keep the genie in
the bottle."

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:13.950
The rocking chair moving on it’s own is
a reminder of Judy’s first unpleasant experience

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:17.330
with Annabelle back in The Conjuring.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.450
"Help!

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.560
Help!

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.680
Dad!"

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.920
"Get away from the door Judy!"

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:29.780
"Oh God!"

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.840
The windvane that moves on its own could tie
back into Annabelle Creation, which took place

00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:38.090
on a farmhouse, but the big thing I noticed
here was this mannequin in the corner wearing

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.090
white robes.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:43.080
The costume is somewhat similar to Sister
Irene’s white garb in The Nun, but it also

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.800
looks like there’s a veil, so maybe it’s
more of a wedding dress type thing.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.840
That'll be something that we have to keep
an eye on when the movie comes out.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.010
Father Gordon from The Conjuring 2 is seen
towards the beginning of the trailer blessing

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:57.909
the room of cursed objects, something that
Ed claims they do for protection back in the

00:02:57.909 --> 00:02:59.040
first movie.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.560
"Doesn't it worry you to have all these items?

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:02.670
Right in your home?"

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.920
"Oh that's why we have a priest who comes
by once a month to bless the room."

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.829
Then we’ve got the typewriter writing on
it’s own, where it says “miss me” over

00:03:09.829 --> 00:03:13.540
and over, just like the three young people
from the opening sequence of The Conjuring

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.019
saw the same message appear on their ceiling.

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:17.080
Noticing a pattern yet?

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.370
A lot of callbacks to the first Conjuring.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:23.170
Let’s add the Bathsheba ankle pulls in the
middle of the night, which also happens to

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.709
the young girls of the Perron family to that
list.

00:03:25.709 --> 00:03:29.530
This demonic looking girl in the trailer seems
to be affected by the this projection cast

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:34.300
onto her, which is footage of one of the exorcisms
that Ed and Lorraine Warren use to teach about

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.739
what they do at the University.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.799
Finally, we have the mystery of this little
girl.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.440
“Can I play with Annabelle?”

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.700
“I think you have the wrong house, there’s
no Annabelle here.”

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.010
“The **** you say to me you little ****?!”

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:52.340
This is Bee, the little girl who died in Annabelle:
Creation who the demon that later went on

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:56.659
to possess the Annabelle doll was masquerading
as in order to trick the family into providing

00:03:56.659 --> 00:03:57.800
her with a human vessel.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.989
It looks like the demon is still using the
form of Bee in modern times, she’s even

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:03.790
still wearing the dress that Bee died in.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:07.530
If you’re not up to date on all the Things
You Missed in the previous movie in the Conjuring

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.689
franchise, click the playlist on the left
to get up to speed on that.

00:04:10.689 --> 00:04:15.010
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week so you don't miss out on

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:18.910
the upcoming Things You Missed episodes on
Annabelle and Annabelle Creation, ring that

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.500
deathbell for notifications and I’ll see
you in the next one.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.569
Assuming we both survive.

